msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1199
msgid "Hides the Comments menu, the Discussion settings page, the dashboard widget, the admin bar bubble and the Recent Comments widget. Applies only when disabling everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1207
msgid "Removes the REST API comment routes, XML-RPC comment/pingback methods, the X-Pingback header and comment feeds. Applies only when disabling everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1215
msgid "Users with these roles (and visitors who are not logged in, when that is ticked) are not affected by \"Disable comments\" or by closing comments on old posts: for them comments, the comment tools in the admin and the REST routes work as in WordPress. The choice is made per request, so a page served from a page cache looks the same to everybody; keep pages with a comment form out of the cache."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1224
msgid "Pingbacks and trackbacks (notices from other sites) can stay on although comments are disabled. Used only while \"Disable comments\" is on; a type that is not ticked is refused. Pingbacks travel through XML-RPC, so they also need \"Disable XML-RPC\" to be off, otherwise pings stay closed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1233
msgid "New comments of these types are refused even where comments are open (for example pingbacks, or product reviews while ordinary comments stay open). Existing comments are not touched. Works without \"Disable comments\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1234
msgid "Product reviews"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1242
msgid "0 = never. Comments and pingbacks are closed on content published more than this many days ago. The module does this itself (it filters whether comments are open); the WordPress option \"Automatically close comments on old posts\" is not changed, so switching the module off restores the earlier state. Existing comments stay visible."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1249
msgid "Disable blog"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1250
msgid "Removes blog features - hides \"Posts\" from the admin menu, redirects blog posts and archives to the homepage and hides the Quick Draft dashboard widget. Suitable for presentation sites without a blog."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1260
msgid "Stops attackers harvesting usernames via ?author=N redirects and the public /wp/v2/users REST route. Logged-in users keep full access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1267
msgid "Delete unused default themes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1268
msgid "Deletes the default Twenty* themes (Twenty Twenty-Four etc.) that WordPress itself brought - with the install or with a core update - and that nothing uses; an unused theme is only extra attack surface. A Twenty* theme that somebody installed by hand (upload, wordpress.org, FTP) is never deleted. Also never touches the active theme, its parent/child, or any theme that is the parent of another installed theme. The newest default theme always stays as the fallback WordPress switches to if the active theme breaks. Runs on save and then at most once a day while you are in the admin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1275
msgid "Hide author slugs"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1276
msgid "Replaces usernames in author archive URLs and REST API responses with an encrypted ID, so the login name cannot be read from the URL. Use instead of or together with blocking user enumeration."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1283
msgid "Disable theme/plugin file editor"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1284
msgid "Defines DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT so nobody can edit theme or plugin PHP from wp-admin - a common way attackers turn a stolen admin login into code execution."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1291
msgid "Harden the login page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1292
msgid "Hides detailed login error messages (so an attacker cannot tell which of username/password was wrong) and disables Application Passwords."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1301
msgid "Enable Upload Guard scanner"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1302
msgid "Checks new uploads and runs a scheduled night scan of uploads, plugins and themes. It only reports - files are never moved or deleted automatically. Plugin files identical to the official WordPress.org version count as clean. Turning this off stops all scanning (existing findings are kept). CSP violation reporting is unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1308
msgid "Full scan frequency"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1309
msgid "Automatic full scans run only at night, in a 4-hour window starting between 01:00 and 03:00 site time (different for each site), in small batches with pauses, and wait when the server is busy. Unchanged files are skipped without being read; every 4th run reads everything. New uploads are always checked right away."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1311
msgid "Weekly (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1313
msgid "Only when I click \"Scan now\""
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1321
msgid "Email admin on detections"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1322
msgid "Sends a throttled summary email when new high/critical findings appear (at most one per 15 minutes)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1329
#: includes/Modules/ServiceRequests/Module.php:134
msgid "Notification email"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1330
msgid "Where to send Upload Guard alerts. Leave blank to use the site admin email."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1337
msgid "Custom patterns (advanced)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1338
msgid "Your own regular expressions for suspicious code, one per line, e.g. /malicious_function\\s*\\(/i. Lines starting with # are comments. Each matching pattern adds 25 points to the file score. Invalid expressions are commented out on save and never used."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1345
msgid "Skipped paths"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1346
msgid "Files under these paths are never scanned, one per line. Either an absolute path or a path relative to the site, e.g. wp-content/plugins/cache-plugin/. Useful for a trusted plugin that legitimately uses eval() or base64_decode()."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1398
msgid "Google Fonts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/Module.php:1399
msgid "Google Tag Manager + Analytics"
msgstr ""

