#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:72
msgid "Login, registration, lost password and comments ask for a quick check before they are accepted. With the key-less Shield the browser of the visitor solves a small puzzle by itself: a fraction of a second, no account, no keys, no cookies, nothing sent to a third party. A visitor without JavaScript answers a simple sum instead, so nobody is locked out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:73
msgid "The Shield stops mass scripted attempts. It does not tell a person from a clever script: an attacker who spends the computing time passes, only slower. A visitor whose browser blocks the script sees the sum after a few seconds. Five wrong answers count as failed logins and lock the address like wrong passwords do."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:74
msgid "When you use Cloudflare Turnstile or reCAPTCHA keys or a CAPTCHA plugin instead, or when you want to protect only the forms of the Forms module."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:75
msgid "A CAPTCHA is already set up (switched on, keys stored or a CAPTCHA plugin active), or the site is behind a reverse proxy that is not Cloudflare: the Shield limits per IP address, and behind such a proxy every visitor looks the same."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:78
msgid "Automatic uses keys from the central application while the site is connected, then your own Turnstile or reCAPTCHA keys, and the key-less Shield when there are none. Anything you choose by hand is used as it is."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:79
msgid "Choosing the Shield on a site that has Turnstile or reCAPTCHA keys drops that check: the Shield is lighter and has no network of other sites behind it. Choosing a provider without its keys switches the CAPTCHA off silently."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:80
msgid "Leave it on Automatic unless you need one specific provider."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:81
msgid "Same as the CAPTCHA switch: a CAPTCHA is already set up, a CAPTCHA plugin is active or the site is behind a reverse proxy that is not Cloudflare."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:84
msgid "Switches comments off on the whole site: the comment forms, the Comments menu and the comment feeds disappear. Existing comments stay in the database but are not shown."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:85
msgid "A site that lives from discussion or from product reviews loses them. With WooCommerce the pack switches comments off on posts and pages only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:86
msgid "When visitors should be able to comment."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:87
msgid "A plugin that disables comments is already active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:90
msgid "After 5 wrong passwords the visitor's IP address is locked out for 15 minutes (longer after repeated lockouts)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:91
msgid "Behind a proxy every visitor looks like the same IP address, so a few typos could lock everybody out. People who share one office address share the limit too."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:92
msgid "When the site is behind a proxy that hides the real IP address and you did not set the IP source in Security > Firewall."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:93
msgid "The site is behind a reverse proxy that is not Cloudflare, or a login protection plugin is active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:96
msgid "Nobody can register or rename a user to a reserved name such as admin, administrator, root or test (any name that contains one of them as a word, for example \"my-admin\")."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:97
msgid "Accounts that already exist are not touched; a new account just cannot take such a name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:98
msgid "When you really need an account with a reserved name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:99
msgid "The login attempt limit is not set (this option works together with it)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:102
msgid "A failed login with a reserved name such as admin locks the IP address at once for the lockout time, without waiting for 5 attempts. Bots try \"admin\" first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:103
msgid "It also applies to a real account with such a name: one typo in its password locks that IP address, maybe your own. Behind a shared proxy address it could lock everybody out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:104
msgid "When an account with a reserved name has to stay, or when you often mistype."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:105
msgid "An existing account uses a reserved name (rename it first), or the login attempt limit is not set."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:108
msgid "The login page no longer tells whether the username or the password was wrong. Application Passwords are switched off, so new ones cannot be created. Messages about a lockout, CAPTCHA and two-step verification stay readable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:109
msgid "Integrations that sign in with an Application Password stop working: the WordPress mobile app, REST clients, some MCP servers and publishing tools."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:110
msgid "When you use such an integration, or want to create Application Passwords again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:111
msgid "Somebody already has an Application Password (the pack never cuts off existing ones)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:114
msgid "Feed addresses (posts, comments, categories, search) answer 403 and the feed links leave the page head."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:115
msgid "RSS readers, newsletter tools with RSS campaigns, podcast apps and aggregators stop getting your updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:116
msgid "When anybody follows the site by RSS or e-mail from the feed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:117
msgid "The site has more than 5 published posts, a feed plugin is active (Mailchimp for WP, podcast or aggregator plugins), or a plugin that disables feeds is active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:120
msgid "The server refuses to hand out wp-config.php and its copies (.bak, .old, .zip, ...), which hold the database password."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:121
msgid "It is a rule in .htaccess, which only Apache and LiteSpeed read. A wrong rule can break the whole site with an HTTP 500, so the pack checks the site afterwards and takes the rules back if it fails."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:122
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:134
msgid "When the server configuration already blocks these files."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:123
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:129
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:135
msgid "The server is not Apache or LiteSpeed (nginx, IIS), or the .htaccess file cannot be written."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:126
msgid "A folder without an index file, for example /wp-content/uploads/, answers 403 instead of showing the list of its files (Options -Indexes)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:127
msgid "On some hosts the setting of .htaccess does not allow the Options line and the site answers HTTP 500. The pack detects it, takes only this line back and keeps the other rules."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:128
msgid "When you offer a file list on purpose."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:132
msgid "readme.html, license.txt and wp-config-sample.php answer 403, so nobody can read the WordPress version from them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:133
msgid "Hardly any. A scanner that reads readme.html to find the version will not see it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:138
msgid "?author=1 no longer redirects to an author page that shows the login name, and the public list of users in the REST API is closed to visitors. Logged-in users keep it. The WordPress users sitemap (wp-sitemap-users.xml) is not changed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:139
msgid "A decoupled front end (headless) or an app that reads authors over the REST API without logging in stops getting them. The block editor and the admin work as before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:140
msgid "When a separate front end or an app needs the public list of users."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:141
msgid "A decoupled front end plugin is active (WPGraphQL, Faust.js, WPGatsby), or a plugin that blocks user enumeration is active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:144
msgid "The user name in the address of an author page (and in the REST \"slug\") is replaced with a code, for example /author/3f9a.../. The old /author/name/ addresses answer 404, there is no redirect. The sitemap and the theme links use the new addresses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:145
msgid "Author pages that are already indexed or linked stop working, and an author sitemap of an SEO plugin changes its addresses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:146
msgid "When you want to keep the old author addresses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:147
msgid "The site has more than 5 published posts (its author pages may already be indexed)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:150
msgid "The old remote interface xmlrpc.php is closed. Attackers use it to guess passwords in bulk."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:151
msgid "Old mobile apps, some publishing tools and the Jetpack connection through XML-RPC stop working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:152
msgid "When a tool you use still talks to xmlrpc.php."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:153
msgid "A plugin that disables XML-RPC is already active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:156
msgid "The WordPress version leaves the page head and the addresses of scripts and styles."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:157
msgid "None noticeable. It only makes automatic scanners work a little harder; it does not replace updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:158
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:212
msgid "Hardly ever needed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:159
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:165
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:201
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:213
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:219
msgid "It is never left out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:162
msgid "The code editors for themes and plugins in wp-admin are switched off (DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT). A stolen administrator login then cannot easily turn into running code."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:163
msgid "You change theme and plugin files over FTP, the file manager or your editor instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:164
msgid "When you edit code in the WordPress admin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:168
msgid "Sends X-Frame-Options (other sites cannot show yours in a frame), X-Content-Type-Options and Referrer-Policy. The headers are set in .htaccess and also by PHP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:169
msgid "A page that has to be shown inside a frame of another site stops appearing there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:170
msgid "When other sites embed your pages on purpose."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:171
msgid "It is never left out; where .htaccess cannot be written the headers are sent by PHP only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:174
msgid "The Permissions-Policy header turns off camera, microphone, location, payment and USB for the page and for frames inside it. It is sent by PHP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:175
msgid "Apple Pay and Google Pay, \"use my location\" on a map and video calls from the page stop working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:176
msgid "When the site needs any of these functions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:177
msgid "WooCommerce is active (online payments), or a plugin that sets the same header is active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:180
msgid "Every request to http:// is redirected to https:// (a rule in .htaccess)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:181
msgid "Behind Cloudflare in the Flexible mode or another proxy that talks to the server over http this causes an endless redirect and the site does not open. The pack checks it and takes the rule back. Insecure content (http images) on a page is blocked by browsers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:182
msgid "When the site does not work over https everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:183
msgid "The site address is not https, this page was not opened over https, plain http does not answer, or the site is behind a proxy that is not Cloudflare."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:186
msgid "Tells the browser to open the site only over https for a whole year, even when somebody types http://."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:187
msgid "The browser remembers it for a year and cannot be talked out of it. If the certificate expires or https breaks, visitors cannot open the site at all until it works again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:188
msgid "Before the site works over https everywhere, including the subdomains."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/SettingHelp.php:189
msgid "The starter pack never switches it on. Switch it on yourself when you are sure about https."
